# Claim: cbor.reader and cbor.writer over files read definite and indefinite containers, chunked text, every float width and integers out to 2^64-1 and -2^64; an item limit fails once and stays failed; the writer sorts encoded keys, a flush does not complete a container, an incomplete finish is sticky, the total limit is checked at the root, and a wider Int is refused; on o0, o1 and o2.
# Hand-derived: the byte fixtures and expected values are the ones Core/Encoding/Cbor.jet checked as in-file tests before the codec stopped naming core.files (D-CORE-LAYERS1=A); each line is printed only after every check in its block held.
fixture: cbor_file_stream_reads_writes_and_keeps_its_limits.fixture
env: NO_COLOR=1
env: JET_STORE_DIR={work}/cache
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O0 run.jet
exit: 0 # o0
stdout: = cbor_file_stream_reads_writes_and_keeps_its_limits.out # o0
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O1 run.jet
exit: 0 # o1
stdout: = cbor_file_stream_reads_writes_and_keeps_its_limits.out # o1
step: jet run --allow=FS.Read,FS.Write -O2 run.jet
exit: 0 # o2
stdout: = cbor_file_stream_reads_writes_and_keeps_its_limits.out # o2
